# Code owners — routes the "require Code Owner review" rule in the main-branch
# ruleset. Later entries win over earlier ones for overlapping paths.
#
# NOTE: the @synchrony-solutions/* teams referenced here must exist and hold
# write (or higher) on this repo before these entries take effect — GitHub
# silently ignores owners it can't resolve. See the Phase 1 team setup:
#   gh api orgs/synchrony-solutions/teams -f name=llopster-maintainers -f privacy=closed
#   gh api orgs/synchrony-solutions/teams -f name=llopster-release -f privacy=closed

# Default: any change needs a maintainer review.
*                     @synchrony-solutions/llopster-maintainers

# Deploy surface: the chart is what customers install — release team owns it.
/helm-chart/          @synchrony-solutions/llopster-release

# CI + repo policy (workflows, this file, dependabot): admin-only review, so a
# compromised or careless write account can't loosen the pipeline that gates it.
# Multiple owners listed so the author of a .github/ PR can always get a
# code-owner review from someone else (self-approval isn't allowed and the
# main-branch ruleset has no bypass). Keep at least two people here; revisit
# this line when admin roles are consolidated (Phase 1 demotion).
/.github/             @braswent @fenimors @jocobtt
